<p id="mwBA"><i id="mwBQ"><b id="mwBg">Sinularia polydactyla</b></i>, known as <b id="mwBw">finger leather coral</b>, is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Species" title="Species" id="mwCA">species</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Octocorallia" title="Octocorallia" id="mwCQ">soft coral</a> in the family Alcyoniidae.<sup about="#mwt6" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-WoRMS_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"WoRMS"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-WoRMS-1"}}'><a href="./Sinularia_polydactyla#cite_note-WoRMS-1" id="mwCg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Bio-active <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Chemical_isolate" title="Chemical isolate" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDg">isolates</a> called durumolides have been found in all samples of this coral.<sup about="#mwt9" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="./Sinularia_polydactyla#cite_note-2" id="mwDw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

